  "intro": [
    "Every EKS operation the emulator advertises, and what Emuplane does with it.",
    "The service is REST/JSON under `/clusters`, signed with the `eks` credential",
    "scope, and has no console action.",
    "A cluster is a record and settles `ACTIVE` whether or not a k3s container came",
    "up, so these tests read and write the control plane rather than a Kubernetes",
    "API. Nodegroups, addons, access entries, access-policy associations, OIDC",
    "identity provider configurations and pod identity associations are records",
    "too; a delete takes its children with it. Two clusters exist because the API",
    "allows one encryption configuration and one OIDC identity provider per cluster."
  ],
